1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,098
9 MINERS WERE TRAPPED 240 FEET UNDERGROUND

2
00:00:04,397 --> 00:00:07,775
TENS OF MILLIONS OF GALLONS OF WATER HAD FLOODED THE MINE

3
00:00:08,075 --> 00:00:11,323
THEIR ONLY HOPE WAS A DRILL, AND TIME WAS RUNNING OUT

4
00:00:11,623 --> 00:00:14,852
THEN, FROM DEEP BELOW, RESCUERS HEARD 9 TAPS

5
00:00:15,452 --> 00:00:17,402
THIS IS THE QUECREEK MINE RESCUE

6
00:00:17,702 --> 00:00:22,373
SOMERSET COUNTY, PENNSYLVANIA · JULY 2002

7
00:00:22,623 --> 00:00:26,452
18 MINERS, IN TWO CREWS OF 9

8
00:00:26,752 --> 00:00:29,471
RIGHT NEXT DOOR WAS AN OLD, ABANDONED MINE

9
00:00:29,771 --> 00:00:32,529
AROUND 9 P.M. ON JULY 24, THEY BROKE INTO IT

10
00:00:33,129 --> 00:00:34,187
WATER POURED IN

11
00:00:34,537 --> 00:00:36,059
ONE CREW OF 9 GOT OUT

12
00:00:36,358 --> 00:00:39,703
THE OTHER 9 WERE CUT OFF 240 FEET DOWN

13
00:00:40,303 --> 00:00:42,638
RESCUERS RACED TO THE SURFACE ABOVE THEM

14
00:00:42,938 --> 00:00:46,927
A MINE SAFETY EXPERT STUDIED MAPS TO PICK THE SPOT

15
00:00:47,227 --> 00:00:51,598
DRILLING BEGAN THE NEXT MORNING

16
00:00:51,898 --> 00:00:54,627
THE FIRST HOLE WAS NARROW, BUT IT COULD BRING AIR

17
00:00:54,927 --> 00:00:58,128
AIR PUMPED DOWN HELPED HOLD BACK THE WATER

18
00:00:58,478 --> 00:01:01,389
BY NOON, THE WATER WAS WITHIN 70 FEET OF THEM

19
00:01:01,989 --> 00:01:03,647
RESCUERS TAPPED ON THE PIPE

20
00:01:03,947 --> 00:01:05,556
THREE STRONG BANGS ANSWERED

21
00:01:05,906 --> 00:01:10,464
9 TAPS: “THERE ARE NINE OF US DOWN HERE”

22
00:01:11,064 --> 00:01:12,984
BUT THE HARDEST PART WAS STILL AHEAD

23
00:01:13,284 --> 00:01:16,558
EARLY ON JULY 26, THE DRILL BIT BROKE

24
00:01:16,858 --> 00:01:20,712
CREWS STARTED A SECOND HOLE WHILE REMOVING THE BIT

25
00:01:21,012 --> 00:01:24,195
BY AFTERNOON, THE BIT WAS OUT AND DRILLING RESUMED

26
00:01:24,795 --> 00:01:28,348
A BIGGER DRILL BROKE THROUGH ON JULY 27

27
00:01:28,648 --> 00:01:32,467
24 INCHES WIDE: JUST BIG ENOUGH FOR A RESCUE CAGE

28
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:35,176
THEN CREWS HEARD THAT ALL 9 WERE ALIVE

29
00:01:35,776 --> 00:01:39,500
A CAGE JUST 22 INCHES WIDE WENT DOWN THE SHAFT

30
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,292
ONE AT A TIME, THE MINERS WERE PULLED UP

31
00:01:42,642 --> 00:01:45,110
BY JULY 28, ALL 9 WERE OUT

32
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:48,292
ABOUT 77 HOURS AFTER THE FLOOD BEGAN

33
00:01:48,642 --> 00:01:49,991
ALL 9 SURVIVED

34
00:01:50,491 --> 00:01:53,917
A FLOODED MINE, A NARROW HOLE, AND 9 TAPS ON A PIPE

35
00:01:54,417 --> 00:01:57,451
NEXT: THE THAI CAVE RESCUE. FOLLOW

